{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++20 (64) code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++20 (64) code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <queue>\n#include <bitset>\n#include <set>\n#include <map>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#define ll long long\n#define INF 0x3f3f3f3f\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst ll p[] = {1, 10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000, 10000000};\nconst int M = 998244353, M2 = 1000000007;\nint idx, ans;\nll n, s[10], Idx = -1;\nint v[10][1000005], L[10];\n\ninline int Del(int x) { return x >= M ? x - M : x; }\ninline int Del1(int x) { return x >= M2 ? x - M2 : x; }\n\nvoid dfs1(int x, int d) {\n    int u = Del(idx - x + M);\n    v[d][L[d]++] = u;\n    ++idx;\n    s[d] += u;\n    if (d == 6) return;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) dfs1(x * 10 + i, d + 1);\n}\n\ninline void query(int x, ll r) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < 7; ++i) {\n        ll t = (r - x * p[i]) % M;\n        if (t < 0) t += M;\n        int g = lower_bound(v[i], v[i] + L[i], M - t) - v[i];\n        ans = (ans + s[i] + t * L[i] - 1ll * M * (L[i] - g)) % M2;\n    }\n}\n\nvoid dfs2(ll x) {\n    if ((x + 1) * p[6] <= n + 1 && x * p[7] > n) {\n        query(x, Idx + 1);\n        Idx += idx;\n        return;\n    }\n    ++Idx;\n    ans = Del1(ans + Del((Idx - x) % M + M));\n    for (int i = (!x); i < 10; ++i)\n        if (x * 10 + i <= n) dfs2(x * 10 + i);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    dfs1(0, 0);\n    cin >> n;\n    dfs2(0);\n    cout << ans << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport bisect\n\np = [1, 10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000, 1000000, 10000000]\nM = 998244353\nM2 = 1000000007\n\nidx = 0\nans = 0\nn = 0\nIdx = -1\ns = [0] * 10\nv = [[] for _ in range(10)]\nL = [0] * 10\n\ndef Del(x):\n    return x - M if x >= M else x\n\ndef Del1(x):\n    return x - M2 if x >= M2 else x\n\ndef dfs1(x, d):\n    global idx, s, v, L\n    u = Del(idx - x + M)\n    v[d].append(u)\n    L[d] += 1\n    idx += 1\n    s[d] += u\n    if d == 6:\n        return\n    for i in range(10):\n        dfs1(x * 10 + i, d + 1)\n\ndef query(x, r):\n    global ans, s, v, L\n    for i in range(7):\n        t = (r - x * p[i]) % M\n        if t < 0:\n            t += M\n        g = bisect.bisect_left(v[i], M - t)\n        ans = (ans + s[i] + t * L[i] - M * (L[i] - g)) % M2\n\ndef dfs2(x):\n    global Idx, ans, n, idx\n    if (x + 1) * p[6] <= n + 1 and x * p[7] > n:\n        query(x, Idx + 1)\n        Idx += idx\n        return\n    Idx += 1\n    ans = Del1(ans + ((Idx - x) % M))\n    start = 0 if x != 0 else 1\n    for i in range(start, 10):\n        if x * 10 + i <= n:\n            dfs2(x * 10 + i)\n\ndef main():\n    global n, ans, idx, Idx, s, v, L\n    dfs1(0, 0)\n    n = int(input().strip())\n    dfs2(0)\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.145764938177308e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0007229813490994275, -0.0006225554971024394, -0.6931494474411011, -2.384